<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Testament</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The New Testament is the second part of the Christian Bible, a collection of 27 books in Greek written in the 1st and early 2nd centuries, including the four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a>, the letters of Paul and Revelation. Its translations shaped many languages: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> translated it into German at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> in 1521–1522, and Danish mission scholars at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharangambadi">Tranquebar</a> published a Tamil version in 1714.</p></div>
